    "Description": "P1b (Hill-attack -> Blueprints migration, EQS request/poll slice, architect Architect_Question_7_EQS_Slice.md): Action_RequestAreaQuery rebuilt as a visually-authored AiPrimitive BTreeAction (Intent=Action, NOT Condition -- this graph must be able to Return(Running) while a request is in flight or the EQS batch is full; a Condition-intent blueprint's bool wrapper (TickCore(...)==NodeStatus.Success) would collapse Running to false and destroy the poll). Graph: EventEntry -> Compare(GetVariable(CachedEqsRequestId), Literal Int64 -1L, NotEqual) -> Branch1. Branch1.True (a request is already in flight): FunctionCall AreaQueryBatchOps.IsReady(requestId<-CachedEqsRequestId) [IsPure, TrailingContext=View] -> Branch2: True -> Return(Success) (result already resolved, advance the sequence); False -> Return(Running) (still polling). Branch1.False (no request in flight): FunctionCall WorldOps.IsAlive(e<-GetParameter(TargetAreaEntity)) [IsPure, TrailingContext=View] -> Branch3: False -> Return(Failure) (covers the oracle's combined IsNull||!IsAlive guard, since WorldOps.IsAlive(Entity.Null,_)==false); True -> FunctionCall AreaQueryBatchOps.Request(targetArea<-GetParameter(TargetAreaEntity)) [IsPure=false/EXEC so the side effect is never dead-code eliminated, TrailingContext=SelfAndView -- self then view auto-appended by Stage5] -> id:Int64 -> Compare(id, Literal Int64 -1L, Equal) -> Branch4: True (EQS batch full) -> Return(Running) (retry next frame, matches oracle's id==-1 guard); False (submitted) -> SetVariable(CachedEqsRequestId<-id) -> FunctionCall WorldOps.SimTime() [IsPure, TrailingContext=View, no visible data-in pin -- the sole parameter is the auto-appended view] -> now:Single -> SetVariable(EqsRequestTime<-now) -> Return(Success). Return(Success) is a shared 2-in-degree merge point (Branch2.True direct path AND the submitted-request tail); Return(Running) is a shared 2-in-degree merge point (Branch2.False AND Branch4.True) -- both are pure exec-In-only terminal sinks, proven safe by HillAssault2_AimAndFireSpecific's 3-/4-in-degree Return merges; Return(Failure) has a single predecessor. GetVariable(CachedEqsRequestId) and GetParameter(TargetAreaEntity) each fan out their single pure Value-Out pin to 2 consumers (pure data nodes may fan out freely; only exec Out pins must remain single-destination). Curated helpers (AreaQueryBatchOps.Request/IsReady, WorldOps.SimTime, per architect Q#7-D): side-effecting Request stays an EXEC FunctionCall so it is never DCE'd; the Running/Success/Failure routing and the batch-full retry stay fully visual. Does not modify the C# oracle (HillAttackCommanderNodes.Action_RequestAreaQuery, line 188-227).",
